sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant Gateway as API Gateway
    participant Booking as Booking Service
    participant Inventory as Inventory Service
    participant Payment as Payment Simulator

    Customer->>Gateway: POST /api/bookings (eventId, seatIds)
    Gateway->>Booking: Create booking for JWT subject
    Booking->>Booking: Save Booking(PENDING)
    Booking->>Inventory: POST /internal/holds (bookingId, seatIds)
    Inventory->>Inventory: Atomically hold all seats
    Inventory-->>Booking: Held seats + prices + expiresAt
    Booking->>Booking: Save BookingItems + total + holdExpiresAt
    Booking->>Booking: Set status HELD
    Booking-->>Customer: Booking HELD + expiry

    Customer->>Gateway: POST /api/bookings/{id}/confirm-payment
    Gateway->>Booking: Explicit customer confirmation
    Booking->>Payment: POST /internal/payments/simulate
    Payment->>Payment: Create or return one simulation per booking
    Payment-->>Booking: SUCCEEDED or FAILED

    alt Payment simulation succeeded
        Booking->>Inventory: POST /internal/holds/{bookingId}/confirm
        alt Hold still active
            Inventory->>Inventory: Mark holds CONFIRMED and seats SOLD
            Inventory-->>Booking: Confirmation successful
            Booking->>Booking: Set status CONFIRMED
            Booking-->>Customer: Booking CONFIRMED
        else Hold expired or cannot be confirmed
            Inventory-->>Booking: Conflict / expired
            Booking->>Inventory: DELETE /internal/holds/{bookingId}
            Booking->>Booking: Set status EXPIRED or FAILED
            Booking-->>Customer: Booking not confirmed
        end
    else Payment simulation failed
        Booking->>Inventory: DELETE /internal/holds/{bookingId}
        Inventory-->>Booking: Active holds released
        Booking->>Booking: Set status FAILED
        Booking-->>Customer: Payment simulation failed
    end
